IMPULSE FALLOFF -- MF8 link, both line codes
  impulses: damped rings, amplitude U(0.5, 3.0) x transmitted peak, 15-80 kHz,
  20-200 us decay, Poisson arrivals.  512 kbps, 1.8 MHz cable, no other
  impairment.  Each rate point is several independent 10 s runs,
  enough for ~200 impulses, clamped to 3-12 runs.
  "muted" is time unlocked after the first lock; "se" its standard error
  across runs; "LOF/imp" is loss-of-frame events per impulse.

